    <!-- 공장 초기화 — 다섯 화면.
         Written out rather than built in the module, unlike 초기화's one
         shared dialog: these five say five different things, so there is
         no wording to keep in step and the sentences that decide whether
         somebody wipes their machine are better read in the markup.

         Each can be left without answering: 취소, the backdrop, Escape.
         The progress one has nothing to cancel and so carries no button
         - it can still be left, and the module refuses to raise the
         screen after it if somebody has. -->

    <!-- 1. What goes, before any password. The facts come first: being
           asked to prove who you are before being told what you are
           agreeing to is how people agree to the wrong thing. -->
    <div class="backdrop" id="dlg-factory-what">
      <div class="modal wide tall appear">
        <h3>공장 초기화</h3>
        <p>이 컴퓨터를 처음 켠 상태로 되돌립니다.</p>

        <div class="sec">지워지는 것</div>
        <div class="list">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>모든 계정과 비밀번호</b></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>홈 폴더의 파일</b><i>문서와 사진, 내려받은 파일</i></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>설치한 앱과 패키지</b></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>네트워크 설정</b><i>저장된 Wi-Fi 와 비밀번호</i></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>모든 설정</b></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>로그와 기록</b></div>
            <div class="vl">지워짐</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The second list is the one that decides whether this is a
             reset or a brick, and it is why the dialog is 460px wide
             instead of ending at the caution. -->
        <div class="sec">남는 것</div>
        <div class="list">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>운영체제</b><i>초기화가 끝나면 이 컴퓨터는 그대로 켜집니다</i></div>
            <div class="vl">남음</div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="lb"><b>부팅 파티션의 SSH 인증 키</b><i>네트워크로만 닿는 컴퓨터에 다시 들어가는 길입니다</i></div>
            <div class="vl">남음</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The operational fact first and the reason after it, because
             the sentence somebody has to act on is the one about the
             power. A caption rather than a paragraph: it is the class
             the owner's own screens end a block with, and it carries
             the gap that a bare <p> after a list does not. -->
        <div class="caption">되돌리는 데 몇 분이 걸리고, 끝날 때까지 전원을 끄지 않아야 합니다. 이 컴퓨터의 루트는 디스크에 있는 ext4 파일 시스템이라 커널 안에 되돌릴 원본이 없고, 부팅 파티션에 둔 사본에서 시스템을 다시 쓰기 때문입니다.</div>

        <div class="note bad">▲ 되돌릴 수 없습니다. 한 번 시작하면 도중에 멈출 수 없습니다.</div>

        <div class="foot">
          <button class="btn quiet pressable" data-close="dlg-factory-what">취소</button>
          <button class="btn pressable" data-go>계속</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. Who you are. Plain, not red: asking for a password is not
           itself the destructive step. -->
    <div class="backdrop" id="dlg-factory-who">
      <div class="modal appear">
        <h3>관리자 확인</h3>
        <p>공장 초기화는 관리자만 할 수 있습니다. 관리자 비밀번호를 입력하면 마지막 확인으로 넘어갑니다.</p>
        <div class="fieldlabel">관리자 비밀번호</div>
        <input class="field" type="password" autocomplete="off" data-pw>
        <div class="inline"></div>
        <div class="foot">
          <button class="btn quiet pressable" data-close="dlg-factory-who">취소</button>
          <button class="btn pressable" data-go disabled>확인</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. Mean it. The standard pattern for something irreversible, and
           the last place where reading the sentence above the field is
           still cheaper than what follows. -->
    <div class="backdrop" id="dlg-factory-sure">
      <div class="modal appear">
        <h3>마지막 확인</h3>
        <p>시작하면 계정과 파일, 설치한 앱이 모두 지워집니다. 되돌릴 수 없습니다.</p>
        <div class="fieldlabel">확인을 위해 초기화라고 입력합니다</div>
        <input class="field" autocomplete="off" placeholder="초기화" data-phrase>
        <div class="foot">
          <button class="btn quiet pressable" data-close="dlg-factory-sure">취소</button>
          <button class="btn danger pressable" data-go disabled>시작</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Doing it. No 취소 button, because by here there is nothing
           left to cancel - and a button that says 취소 and cannot is
           worse than none. Amber on the power line: it is a constraint
           while the work runs, not a failure. -->
    <div class="backdrop" id="dlg-factory-run">
      <div class="modal appear">
        <h3>공장 초기화</h3>
        <p>초기화가 진행 중입니다.</p>
        <div class="prog"></div>
        <div class="caption" data-step></div>
        <div class="note">▲ 끝날 때까지 전원을 끄지 않아야 합니다.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. Done. The SSH line is repeated here rather than left in the
           first dialog: this is the screen somebody reads while
           wondering whether they have just locked themselves out of a
           machine they cannot reach. -->
    <div class="backdrop" id="dlg-factory-done">
      <div class="modal appear">
        <h3>초기화를 마쳤습니다</h3>
        <p>이 컴퓨터가 곧 다시 시작합니다. 다시 켜지면 처음 켰을 때와 같은 첫 화면이 나옵니다.</p>
        <p>부팅 파티션의 SSH 인증 키는 그대로 있습니다. 네트워크로 들어오던 방법은 초기화 뒤에도 같습니다.</p>
        <div class="foot">
          <button class="btn primary pressable" data-close="dlg-factory-done">확인</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>